---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import portrait from '../images/alex-portrait.jpeg';
import family from '../images/family.jpeg';
import otis from '../images/otis.jpeg';
import meredithAndFiru from '../images/meredith-and-firu.jpeg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Alex Partida is a web developer and designer in Los Angeles. Apparel production manager turned developer, on the web team of a daily newspaper, building sites for small businesses and independent practitioners."
  showHome={true}
>
  <div class="about">
    <!-- The portrait bleeds off the right edge, as it did originally. -->
    <Image
      src={portrait}
      alt="Alex Partida"
      class="about__portrait"
      widths={[320, 480, 720]}
      sizes="(max-width: 860px) 40vw, 360px"
      loading="eager"
    />

    <div class="column about__col">
      <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
      <p class="quote">From Apparel to Tech</p>

      <div class="prose about__prose">
        <p>
          Hi 👋 — welcome to my portfolio. I'm an apparel production manager
          turned web developer. Before I wrote software I ran production in Los
          Angeles: schedules, vendors, margins, and the specific stress of a
          deadline that cannot move. I changed careers through a six-month
          coding bootcamp and a web development certificate at UC Davis
          Extension, and I've been building for the web professionally since
          2021.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm a web developer at <strong>The Salt Lake Tribune</strong>, a
          nonprofit daily newspaper. I migrated their newsletter platform from
          Mailchimp to Iterable, build the subscription, donation and
          sponsorship features that fund the newsroom, and work on the bill
          tracker readers use to follow the Utah legislature. The Tribune being
          a nonprofit makes the work feel like it matters, and shipping to an
          audience that notices the moment something breaks is a good education.
        </p>
        <p>
          Alongside that I take on a small number of freelance projects for
          small businesses and independent practitioners — a yoga teacher, a tax
          practice, people whose website is a real part of how they make a
          living rather than a brochure. Because I keep the list short, the work
          gets proper attention.
        </p>

        <h2>How the production background shows up</h2>
        <p>
          Running production teaches you that the handoff is the whole job. A
          beautiful sample means nothing if the factory can't reproduce it, and
          a beautiful website means nothing if its owner can't change the
          opening hours.
        </p>
        <p>
          So that's what I optimise for. The most interesting decision on a
          recent project wasn't the design — it was putting the client's class
          schedule in a Google Sheet she owns, so she posts her own dates from
          her phone without calling me. Every project ends with documentation
          written for the person who has to use it.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm skilled in HTML, CSS, JavaScript, React, WordPress and Adobe
          Photoshop, and I care a lot about sites being fast and accessible —
          less a moral position than a practical one. A slow site on a phone on
          a bad connection is a site nobody reads. Have a look at my <a
            href="/work">work</a
          > or find me on <a href="https://github.com/alpartida">GitHub</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Away from the keyboard</h2>
        <p>
          I live in Los Angeles with my partner Zach and my daughter Surie. We
          are outnumbered by animals — Otis the miniature poodle, Meredith Grey
          the Nebelung, and Firulais, who turned up on the patio one day, got
          fed once by my daughter, and never left. All three were adopted, two
          of them by accident.
        </p>
        <p>
          Weekends are horses, the piano in the living room, and all four of us
          reading completely different books in the same room. Learning to code
          changed my life in the obvious ways, and also in one I didn't expect: I
          met Zach on the way through it. My daughter watches her mom work in a
          field without many women in it, which I think about more than I
          expected to.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="gallery">
        <figure>
          <Image
            src={family}
            alt="Alex with her family in Los Angeles"
            widths={[320, 560, 760]}
            sizes="(max-width: 760px) 90vw, 340px"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <Image
            src={otis}
            alt="Otis, a miniature poodle"
            widths={[320, 560]}
            sizes="(max-width: 760px) 44vw, 230px"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <Image
            src={meredithAndFiru}
            alt="Meredith Grey and Firulais, two rescued cats"
            widths={[320, 560]}
            sizes="(max-width: 760px) 44vw, 230px"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
      </div>

      <p class="about__cv-note">
        For a full list of my work experience, download my résumé below.
      </p>
      <div class="cluster about__actions">
        <a href="/AlexPartidaResume.pdf" class="btn" download>My CV</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="link-u about__link">Start a project</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    position: relative;
  }

  .about__col {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  /* Originally absolutely positioned and bleeding off the right. Kept,
     but clipped to the viewport so it can't create a scrollbar. */
  .about__portrait {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    right: calc(var(--gutter) * -1);
    width: min(360px, 34vw);
    height: auto;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .about__prose,
  .about__col .quote {
    max-width: 44ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .about__portrait {
      width: 38vw;
      opacity: 0.55;
      right: 0;
    }

    .about__prose,
    .about__col .quote {
      max-width: none;
    }
  }

  .gallery {
    margin-top: var(--s-5);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-2);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(13rem, 1fr));
  }

  .gallery img {
    border: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule-soft);
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
  }

  .about__cv-note {
    margin-top: var(--s-5);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .about__actions {
    margin-top: var(--s-3);
  }

  .about__link {
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
</style>
